From 019399cf9e8f9ce923906f402bc360e113c805b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshkamdar67 <harshkamdar67@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:28:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/32] ggml, vulkan: fused Inkling 2 loop message gate

GGML_OP_INKLING_LOOP_GATE computes cur*(1 - tanh(forget*d)) + tanh(gain*d)*msg with
d = down*[rms_norm(cur); rms_norm(msg)] in one op instead of about twelve. Vulkan runs it in
two passes (the down projection over rank x tokens workgroups, then the outputs) using scratch
rows after the result; the CPU reference fills the same rows. Inkling 2 uses it for batches of
up to 16 tokens. B60 decode 34.4 -> 36.0 tok/s; wikitext-2 PPL at ubatch 16 6.6134 -> 6.6072.
